            <ArticleTitle>[The use of clofelin in the acute period of myocardial infarct].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Data are reported on the action of intravenous clophelin in 30 patients administered within the first 24 hours of myocardial infarction. The agent exhibited a significant analgetic effect, sedative action and normalized the main hemodynamic values. The effect of clophelin on the hemodynamics depended on its initial state. The possibility is shown to predict the pain-killing and hemodynamic effects of the drug by the initial response.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
